## Flow-Specific Component Patterns

### 1. Cultural Intelligence Components
```dart
// Bengali-first text components
class FlowText extends StatelessWidget {
  final String bengali;
  final String english;
  final String? arabic;
  final TextStyle? style;
  
  const FlowText({
    super.key,
    required this.bengali,
    required this.english,
    this.arabic,
    this.style,
  });
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final culturalContext = context.watch(culturalContextProvider);
    final text = _getLocalizedText(culturalContext);
    
    return Text(
      text,
      style: style ?? _getCulturalStyle(culturalContext),
    );
  }
  
  String _getLocalizedText(CulturalContext context) {
    switch (context.locale.languageCode) {
      case 'bn': return bengali;
      case 'hi': return english; // Hindi uses English for now
      case 'ar': return arabic ?? english;
      default: return english;
    }
  }
  
  TextStyle _getCulturalStyle(CulturalContext context) {
    return TextStyle(
      fontFamily: context.isBengali ? 'Hind Siliguri' : 'Inter',
      fontSize: 16,
    );
  }
}
```

### 2. Speed-Optimized Components
```dart
// Quick-add components for fast expense entry
class QuickAddButton extends StatelessWidget {
  final double amount;
  final String category;
  final String paymentMethod;
  final VoidCallback onTap;
  
  const QuickAddButton({
    super.key,
    required this.amount,
    required this.category,
    required this.paymentMethod,
    required this.onTap,
  });
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return GestureDetector(
      onTap: () {
        // Start timer for speed tracking
        ExpenseTimer.start();
        onTap();
      },
      child: Container(
        padding: EdgeInsets.all(12),
        decoration: BoxDecoration(
          color: FlowColors.mintTeal,
          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),
        ),
        child: Column(
          children: [
            Text(
              '৳${_formatAmount(amount)}',
              style: TextStyle(
                fontSize: 18,
                fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                color: Colors.white,
              ),
            ),
            Text(
              category,
              style: TextStyle(
                fontSize: 14,
                color: Colors.white70,
              ),
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
  
  String _formatAmount(double amount) {
    // Use Bengali numerals for speed
    return _convertToBengaliNumerals(amount.toStringAsFixed(0));
  }
}
```

### 3. Empathetic Messaging Components
```dart
// Non-judgmental error and feedback components
class FlowMessage extends StatelessWidget {
  final String bengali;
  final String english;
  final MessageType type;
  
  const FlowMessage({
    super.key,
    required this.bengali,
    required this.english,
    required this.type,
  });
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final culturalContext = context.watch(culturalContextProvider);
    final text = _getLocalizedText(culturalContext);
    final color = _getMessageColor();
    
    return Container(
      padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),
      decoration: BoxDecoration(
        color: color.withOpacity(0.1),
        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),
        border: Border.all(color: color.withOpacity(0.3)),
      ),
      child: Row(
        children: [
          Icon(_getMessageIcon(), color: color),
          SizedBox(width: 12),
          Expanded(
            child: Text(
              text,
              style: TextStyle(color: color),
            ),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
  
  String _getLocalizedText(CulturalContext context) {
    switch (context.locale.languageCode) {
      case 'bn': return bengali;
      default: return english;
    }
  }
  
  Color _getMessageColor() {
    switch (type) {
      case MessageType.success: return FlowColors.success;
      case MessageType.warning: return FlowColors.warning;
      case MessageType.error: return FlowColors.danger;
      case MessageType.info: return FlowColors.trustBlue;
    }
  }
  
  IconData _getMessageIcon() {
    switch (type) {
      case MessageType.success: return Icons.check_circle;
      case MessageType.warning: return Icons.warning;
      case MessageType.error: return Icons.error;
      case MessageType.info: return Icons.info;
    }
  }
}

enum MessageType { success, warning, error, info }
```

## Design System Guidelines

### 1. Consistent Spacing
Use the responsive spacing system:

```dart
Padding(
  padding: context.layout.insetsSymmetric(h: 2, v: 1),
  child: child,
)
```

### 2. Responsive Sizing
Use responsive sizing for different devices:

```dart
Container(
  width: context.layout.responsiveSize(
    phone: 100,
    tablet: 150,
    desktop: 200,
  ),
)
```

### 3. Theme Integration
Always use theme colors and styles:

```dart
Container(
  color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary,
  child: Text(
    'Hello',
    style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.headlineSmall,
  ),
)
```

### 4. Accessibility
Ensure components are accessible:

```dart
Semantics(
  label: 'Save button',
  hint: 'Tap to save the transaction',
  child: AppButton(
    text: 'Save',
    onPressed: () {},
  ),
)
```

## Component Development Guidelines

### 1. File Organization
- Keep related components in the same file
- Use descriptive file names: `app_bars.dart`, `buttons.dart`
- Export components in category files

### 2. Naming Conventions
- Use `App` prefix for main components: `AppButton`, `AppDialog`
- Use descriptive names: `CustomAppBar`, `OptimizedListView`
- Use enums for component variants: `AppButtonStyle`, `AppButtonSize`

### 3. Props and Parameters
- Use required parameters for essential props
- Provide sensible defaults for optional parameters
- Use named parameters for clarity

### 4. Documentation
- Document all public components
- Include usage examples
- Document available variants and options

### 5. Testing
- Test all component variants
- Test responsive behavior
- Test accessibility features